<bx:output>
<div class="container py-5">
	<div class="c-project-hero">
		<p class="c-project-hero__eyebrow">Project</p>
		<h1 class="c-project-hero__title">bx-graphql</h1>
		<p class="c-project-hero__tagline">A schema-agnostic GraphQL server for native <a href="https://boxlang.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-post-link">BoxLang</a>, wrapping <a href="https://www.graphql-java.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-post-link">graphql-java</a> (vendored, v26.0). Write <code>.graphqls</code> files, annotate the classes you already have, or both; it hands back a plain <code>{data, errors}</code> struct. No ColdBox, no WireBox, no HTTP framework required. It's the pure-BoxLang sibling to <a href="/projects/coldbox-graphql" class="c-post-link">coldbox-graphql</a>.</p>
		<div class="c-project-hero__actions">
			<a href="/projects/bx-graphql/docs/getting-started" class="btn btn-primary-custom">Read the Docs</a>
			<a href="https://github.com/robertz/bx-graphql" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline-custom">View on GitHub</a>
			<a href="https://github.com/robertz/bx-graphql-demo" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline-custom">Run the Demo</a>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="c-project-features">
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-code"></i> Schema-first</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">Point <code>schemaPaths</code> at a directory of <code>.graphqls</code> files. A resolver class is only needed for fields with logic; the rest are read off a struct or a class instance.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-magic"></i> Code-first</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">Mark beans <code>@graphqlType</code> and service functions <code>@graphqlQuery</code> or <code>@graphqlMutation</code>. The schema is generated and each field is wired straight to its method.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-shield-lock"></i> Built for real APIs</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body"><code>@graphqlRequires</code> authorization, batch loaders for N+1 lookups, custom scalars with <code>DateTime</code> and <code>Long</code> built in, interfaces, unions and spec-shaped errors.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-boxes"></i> Zero framework</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">A global <code>bxGraphQL()</code> BIF, registered when the module loads. <code>execute()</code> never touches HTTP, so <code>POST /graphql</code> belongs to whatever router your app uses.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<p class="c-post-sidebar__label mb-3 mt-4">Quick start</p>
	<div class="c-post__body c-docs-body">
<pre class="bx-code"><span class="bx-code-label">bash</span><code>box install bx-graphql</code></pre>
<pre class="bx-code"><span class="bx-code-label">bxs</span><code>graphQLService = bxGraphQL( {
	"schemaPaths"         : [ expandPath( "/graphql/schema" ) ],
	"resolverBasePackage" : "models.resolvers"
} )

result = graphQLService.execute(
	query          = '{ widget(id: "1") { name } }',
	queryVariables = {},
	context        = ""
)
// result == { "data" : { "widget" : { "name" : "..." } }, "errors" : [] }</code></pre>
		<p>Or generate the schema from annotated classes, with no <code class="bx-inline">.graphqls</code> files at all:</p>
<pre class="bx-code"><span class="bx-code-label">bxs</span><code>graphQLService = bxGraphQL( {
	"modelPaths"   : [ expandPath( "models/beans" ) ],
	"servicePaths" : [ expandPath( "models/services" ) ]
} )</code></pre>
	</div>
	<p class="mt-3"><a href="/projects/bx-graphql/docs/getting-started" class="c-post-link">Install, settings and both ways to describe a schema &rarr;</a></p>
</div>
</bx:output>
